IMPORTANT: These changes apply ONLY to the UAE credentialing flow. Do not modify any US, UK, or other country flows. Do not change the Therapy, Dietetics, or Physiotherapy flows in any way. Only add and adjust logic specific to a new "Doctor" service within the existing UAE form.

CONTEXT
I have an existing 14-step UAE credentialing form for Therapy (with Dietetics and Physiotherapy as other service options). The form is built as a multi-step wizard with a left sidebar showing progress (steps 1–14) and a right panel rendering each step. I need to make this form dynamically support a new primary service: Doctor, with sub-specialization selection. All changes below are scoped exclusively to the UAE Doctor flow.

CHANGE 1 — Step 1: Service Selection
Add a new selectable card to the existing Service Selection step (Step 1 of 14) with the following content:

Title: Doctor
Subtitle: Medical and surgical healthcare services
This card should appear as the first option in the list, above Therapy.
Selecting "Doctor" should set service = "doctor" in global form state.
All existing cards (Therapy, Dietetics, Physiotherapy) must remain exactly as they are.


CHANGE 2 — Insert New Step 1B (Doctor-only): Specialization Selection
When service === "doctor", inject a new step immediately after Step 1 (before Emirate & Authority Selection). This step should:

